WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.580
Its kind of common for youtubers to start
of videos that might be a little bit spicy

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.780
by saying things like, ' this video is so
hard to make' and I guess that is a little

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.980
bit true here in the fact that I am a little
bit worried about making this video because

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.910
I am afraid of being judged or of letting
anyone down.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:26.180
But I also feel pretty confident in what i'm
doing so i'd just like to explain my situation

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.199
to you.

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:32.480
Maybe sometimes people follow a path something
like this from student to professor.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.450
I've got professor up there because it is
like the pinnacle of the academic pathway.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:43.160
But sometimes maybe a path looks more like
this between those same destinations.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.809
I have always throughout my life been going
on this path, this straight trajectory.

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:55.350
I've always done things that I feel were quite
obviously seen as going forwards in the right

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:57.730
direction towards some goal.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:04.970
Although right now I feel i'm on here and
I think maybe i'm going off somewhere like

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:05.970
this.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:14.350
So I have withdrawn from my PhD program and
I don't even know if i'm going on a path to

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.220
professor which used to be the old destination
or if i'm going to end up somewhere completely

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.689
different and maybe i'm ok with that.

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:28.670
Coming to this decision to withdraw from my
PhD program was actually pretty difficult

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:35.470
and I think the main emotional strain that
I felt was that for the first time in my life

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:39.130
I was unsure of what I wanted to do.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:44.619
I mean this in terms of career because i'd
always been going to the same destination

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:50.020
which maybe was wanting to be a professor
or teaching at a university level.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:57.110
However I started to not enjoy my PhD that
much and I also felt a little bit disillusioned

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.130
with the academic system as a whole.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:09.140
I guess what I felt was for the first time
this unsure feeling of where I wanted to be

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.220
and it was almost overwhelming because it
meant that I could do anything I wanted to

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.220
do.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.420
If I stopped aiming for this one thing then
I could pick any other random thing to aim

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:21.880
for and that was almost overwhelming in a
way.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:25.920
In a good way like that there were so many
possibilities that I could do.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:32.500
I only officially withdrew from the PhD program
in january even though i've known for a while

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.620
that it's what I wanted to do.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.750
And I didn't want to make a video about it
before it was official incase anyone involved

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.090
saw the video and got a bit surprised.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:48.060
In terms of where I was in the program, I
was about a year into the research component

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.000
of doing a PhD.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.690
I, to finish the PhD, probably would have
had to stay doing that for another 2 plus

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.020
years, maybe 2 or 3 maximum.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:04.890
I didn't need to do anymore coursework or
exams it was only research and writing the

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.950
thesis that I needed to do to get the PhD.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:15.440
And so it kind of seems like oh you were so
close why didn't you just stay, but the reasons

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.650
why I wanted to leave, I guess there are lots
of reasons and i'm just going to keep talking

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:27.480
until I feel like most of them have come out,
I just felt like it was the best decision

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:28.519
for me to leave.

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:33.239
Even though in the grand scheme of things
i was kind of close to finishing.

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:38.160
I kind of toyed with the idea of leaving in
my mind for a little while but I didnt think

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:45.200
I would actually be brave enough to do that
because it seemed a bit extreme but i kind

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:51.319
of remember one day just cycling to uni and
i don't know it would like like 20 minutes,

00:03:51.319 --> 00:03:57.630
15 minutes and I felt like my bike would just
get heavier and heavier the closer I got.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.769
In a way that I just felt unmotivated to arrive.

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:09.550
And it was sort of this general feeling that
I would go to uni and be there for a while

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:15.290
but really I just wanted to go home and work
on things that I actually really enjoyed.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:20.759
So YouTube is one of them but I mean there
were sort of a lot of little side projects

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:27.470
I enjoyed doing and I felt like I was torn
and I was separating my time between working

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:30.710
on my PhD and working on the things I actually
liked.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:36.590
Where it got to the point where it kind of
felt unsustainable and kind of inauthentic

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:39.560
to try to work on both at the same time.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:45.840
So ultimately I decided to get rid of the
thing that I didn't enjoy doing and just to

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.009
do the things that I do enjoy.

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:53.810
Sure I could have just kept going and just
stuck at it and in fact a lot of sort of more

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:59.250
senior PhD students maybe they're in their
third or even fourth year of research, i'd

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:04.810
spoken to them a bit and there was this general
sentiment, almost every one of them said 'oh

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:10.490
those feelings are normal for a PhD student,
wait till you get to third or fourth year,

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.690
then you will really feel like you don't want
to be here'.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:18.160
But i thought ok sure like a lot of people
have said that, you get to a point where you

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.550
feel a bit disillusioned with everything and
almost everyone apparently wants to pull out

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:27.389
at some point during the PhD but why should
that be normal?

00:05:27.389 --> 00:05:33.520
And I thought well if im feeling like this
already one year in well how am I going to

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.840
be feeling three years in?

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:40.040
I don't want to be three years in feeling
this because then I dont really have the option

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:46.180
to leave and just leave it all behind but
at my current point I feel like the sooner

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:52.100
the better in the sense that I could just
leave and I wouldnt lose too much effort and

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.160
investment into this thing.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:06:01.319
I would hate to be leaving further into the
PhD so yeah if I was dragging my feet to sort

00:06:01.319 --> 00:06:07.970
of get to uni each day then I think that it
was good to just actually do something that

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:09.110
I was excited about.

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:15.100
I also did a bit of reflecting during this
time and I came to the conclusion that everything

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:20.990
in my life that ive done that ive been quite
proud of came as the result of doing something

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:21.990
brave.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:27.100
So really stepping out of my comfort zone
or just making a decision that wasn't the

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.490
easy one.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:33.800
Doing things like that had got me to the point
that I was at and actually i felt like it

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.690
had been a while since i'd done anything brave
or not taken the easy road.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:44.710
Maybe starting the PhD in the first place
was taking the easy road for me.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:50.599
I know it sort of sounds strange to say that
about pursuing a PhD but after i'd finished

00:06:50.599 --> 00:06:57.270
my undergrad and things it was kind of the
most readily available thing and I had a scholarship

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:02.039
to do it, it was actually the path of least
resistance to just keep going in academia.

00:07:02.039 --> 00:07:08.199
So when i think about this decision it is
quite brave for me to leave academia and try

00:07:08.199 --> 00:07:10.400
to do some other things for a while.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.110
A totally separate reason was kind of highlighted
for me in the form of a youtube comment left

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:20.220
on one of my videos, now im going to read
it out and this was posted on my fortnite

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:25.770
video and I kind of owe this guy a reply so
i'm gonna do that here in this video.

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:32.690
So Basketball guy commented on my video "This
is fairly off topic for this video, but based

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:37.650
on your earlier videos it seems like you got
interested in physics because you got interested

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:43.289
in as you said those big questions like 'what
is our place in the universe?'

00:07:43.289 --> 00:07:48.139
Do you feel like you are still pursuing the
answers to those questions by studying plant

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:50.050
cell physiology?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:56.009
I would have thought you would end up in theoretical
physics trying to understand the standard

00:07:56.009 --> 00:08:02.419
model or trying to quantize gravity or study
GR or doing something like experimental quantum

00:08:02.419 --> 00:08:08.370
mechanics." and I replied to this guy and
I just said this comment hits too close to

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:11.310
home and he said i'd love to here the full
story.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:16.889
So maybe this is a little bit of the full
story in maybe I did start to feel like maybe

00:08:16.889 --> 00:08:25.500
the topic of my PhD which was experimental
biophysics was maybe deviating a bit from

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:30.450
where I saw my greatest passion in physics.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:33.840
Maybe i started to feel like it wasn't really
truly me.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.029
And I don't know how much that is true because
I did actually quite enjoy that project.

00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:45.740
I do enjoy asking those big questions like
you know what is out there in the universe

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:51.970
and what is our place in it and physics offers
some answers to those questions but you're

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:55.480
probably never going to answer questions like
that in the scope of a PhD.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:00.880
That's sort of a romantic idea of a PhD student,
what their life would be like and what they're

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:01.880
working on.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:06.560
Often students are working on you know quite
obscure little elements of physics, maybe

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.730
they fit into this bigger picture of what
physics is.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:17.320
I liked that I was using physics and applying
it to biology and looking at these tiny little

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:21.180
structures and i guess try and find out the
secrets of how they're working.

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:24.720
I did enjoy that but i guess that comment
is right.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:32.760
I guess when I think about my future in physics
and how i got into it i kind of do like the

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.200
idea of working in theoretical physics or
quantum mechanics or stuff like that.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:43.620
So whilst maybe i agree that every PhD student
wants to leave at some point and loses motivation,

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:50.640
maybe the ones that stay it's because they
have that really fundamental motivation in

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.910
what they're doing and it really is exactly
what they picture themselves doing and theyre

00:09:55.910 --> 00:10:01.070
moving towards answering these big questions
in their own mind and that allows them to

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:04.860
have the motivation to stay even when it's
really tough.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.890
I think my problem is also just that I am
interested in so many things.

00:10:09.890 --> 00:10:16.899
I think there is so many different projects
I could do for a PhD that picking one of them

00:10:16.899 --> 00:10:23.690
you will always be unsatisfied that you didn't
pick any number of the other ones.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:28.220
Because it is just really hard to decide what
you want to work on when the scope is so large.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:35.020
In terms of my academic future I wouldn't
rule out returning to a PhD program at some

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.200
point, just not right now.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:44.180
I think right now for me there are other opportunities,
one of them is Youtube but it's not the only

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.959
one, that have a lot more momentum for me
than the PhD.

00:10:47.959 --> 00:10:52.660
So yeah I can kind of see myself finishing
a PhD in the future but what the topic will

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:54.970
be on really I have no idea.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:59.580
People who were critical of my decision said
to me that you know you should just get the

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:05.050
PhD because that qualification will last forever
and YouTube might not be around forever and

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:10.329
I fully agree with that I dont think YouTube
will be around forever, I actually am not

00:11:10.329 --> 00:11:15.490
that optimistic it will be around in the same
way that it is for very long at all.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:21.420
Like even a few years into the future I find
it very hard t predict you know how people

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:24.720
will be learning and what people will be using.

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:29.149
Maybe it will still be YouTube but maybe it
will be something else entirely.

00:11:29.149 --> 00:11:33.920
And that's actually kind of the point, is
that I fell like the universities and the

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:40.519
PhD system is going to be around a lot longer
than YouTube is so I should jump on doing

00:11:40.519 --> 00:11:47.320
YouTube now while I have the opportunity and
I can go back to the PhD later because it

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:49.000
is still going to be there.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:55.890
So really right now I just want to make videos
full-time for YouTube I think that I've seen

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.690
so much power in education on YouTube.

00:11:59.690 --> 00:12:05.399
It's how i learnt it's how I taught myself
things and I think it's how people are learning

00:12:05.399 --> 00:12:06.399
these days.

00:12:06.399 --> 00:12:11.550
Not just learning but also gaining inspiration
and new ideas and connecting with other people

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:15.510
and actually working on awesome projects that
excite me.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:20.810
When you compare that with the academic learning
system, I much prefer Youtube.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:27.610
I dont know I used to want to teach at the
university system and that was you know why

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:33.950
I was going off to this destination of professor
but really I am so much more excited by the

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.320
reach that you can get online.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:41.430
Just in a video made in your bedroom you could
reach a million people, you could never really

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:46.700
reach that same sort of audience teaching
in a conventional environment.

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:52.019
And maybe it's not as impactful if you're
just you know talking through a video but

00:12:52.019 --> 00:12:57.950
I actually find it more impactful because
you guys get to know me and the people that

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:03.820
I watch on YouTube, I feel sort of connected
to them in a way that i don't feel when i'm

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:05.950
learning in a conventional place.

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:12.709
I'm also doing a little bit of freelance science
communication work and in general just pursuing

00:13:12.709 --> 00:13:14.740
the projects that i'm interested in.

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:21.529
I am interested in like start-ups and that
sort of community and so maybe I would like

00:13:21.529 --> 00:13:23.880
to make my own business.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:29.029
Probably based around education and online
education but we will see what happens there.

00:13:29.029 --> 00:13:33.959
I haven't got any solid plans at the moment
that's just something that I know I'd really

00:13:33.959 --> 00:13:34.959
enjoy.

00:13:34.959 --> 00:13:39.760
While I have this momentum in this science
communication aspect of my life at the moment

00:13:39.760 --> 00:13:43.139
I just want to run with it and see where we
go.

00:13:43.139 --> 00:13:48.889
It was a bit of a risky decision for me to
just quit my PhD and I felt a bit like it

00:13:48.889 --> 00:13:54.080
was metaphorically jumping off a cliff because
i was sort of jumping into the unknown.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:58.670
I'm still floundering in the unknown a little
bit, especially because these projects that

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:05.360
I want to work on are still in their infancy
but I do have confidence and i'm happy with

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:08.860
what i'm doing so yea i'm just going to keep
doing it.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:13.690
When I did decide to do this I was really
scared of disappointing people.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:18.760
The number one person I was scared of disappointing
was my PhD supervisor and I guess it took

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:24.050
me multiple meetings with her to actually
work up the courage to say that I wanted to

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:25.339
leave.

00:14:25.339 --> 00:14:27.550
That's because she was a really good supervisor.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:33.810
But I think that fact was reflected in what
her response was which was that she was excited

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:40.579
for me and um after a while like she said
that she felt like her job as a supervisor

00:14:40.579 --> 00:14:46.089
was done that she'd you know set me off on
a path to doing something i enjoyed and that

00:14:46.089 --> 00:14:50.240
was so nice and i guess so perfect to what
I wanted to hear.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:56.620
And i feel like that really was the goal of
a supervisor to get their students you know

00:14:56.620 --> 00:15:03.010
to a pathway to a job to do something that
they enjoy so yea i guess i didn't need to

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:04.300
be so afraid there.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:10.630
There was other people that I was afraid of
disappointing too, I did have this quite fancy

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:17.820
PhD scholarship from one of the banks in Australia,
Westpac, and I was kind of afraid of what

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:22.120
would happen when I told them that I was leaving
the program that they'd like been giving me

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:29.420
money to do but actually they were really
supportive as well and when i told them that

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:34.550
i'd quit, they actually were like oh can we
write an article about you and what you're

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:40.360
doing now because that's so exciting and so
just this week they published an article about

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:41.750
my YouTube channel.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.600
So im like well maybe I didn't need to be
so worried.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:51.740
Um the only other people that i'm really worried
about disappointing is you guys because sometimes

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:58.490
I get comments saying like that i'm someone's
inspiration in terms of pursuing physics or

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:04.110
maths or whatever and I dont know how much
of that inspiration comes from the fact that

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:08.490
i'm a PhD student and that you know that's
my current title.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:14.910
I guess this doesn't change anything of like
my knowledge or what i've done or achieved

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:21.690
in the past but I felt sort of afraid that
people would no longer find me as inspirational.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:29.570
But really I want to be authentic with people
here on Youtube and I want you to know that

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:36.459
I am also a student just like you and so I
have my own things to figure out as well.

00:16:36.459 --> 00:16:42.589
You know I get asked a lot of questions to
do with um giving advice on picking majors

00:16:42.589 --> 00:16:48.920
or picking courses or anything like this as
if I am you know up on a pedestal handing

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.310
out advice because I know the perfect way
to do everything but that's so far from the

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:54.310
truth.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:58.230
I only have my own experience and i'm still
figuring things out too.

00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:04.480
So I want you to know that I have flaws as
well so you can watch my journey here but

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:09.760
you know it is a journey so i'm not at that
destination yet I feel.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:14.110
If I had a time machine and could go a few
years into the future and already have my

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:18.819
PhD degree and already have the qualification
and I think well what would I do with it,

00:17:18.819 --> 00:17:24.720
what I would want to do is exactly what im
doing right here right now.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:32.750
So i'm really grateful to have you watching
and to have this way to provide educational

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.750
content.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:36.760
it's something that I really appreciate and
I really enjoy.

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:41.870
Because i'm already doing exactly what I want
to do right now, that's why I felt like I

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.470
didnt need my PhD degree.

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:49.870
But you know, i know that people's minds change,
i'll see how I feel in a few more years maybe.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:56.160
Thank you so much for your support, from here
if anything things will be the same but i'll

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:59.701
be uploading more content, hopefully better
content, thank you for sticking around and

00:17:59.701 --> 00:18:01.100
thanks for watching :)

